-- title:
--   Norm-one local lift congruent to c modulo N
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $q,q'$ be primes such that the quaternion algebra $B=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`, i.e. $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completion $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division ring (every nonzero element is a unit) precisely when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq B$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $B$ over $\mathbb Q$, is finitely generated, and any order containing it equals it. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ with $q\notin v$ and $q'\notin v$, let $N\in\mathbb N$ with $N\in v$, and let $c\in\Lambda$ and $k\in\mathbb Z$ satisfy $\mathrm{nrd}(c)=1+Nk$, where $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-ax_I^2-bx_J^2+abx_K^2$. Then there is an element $s$ of [`Submodule.localBox Λ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive subgroup of $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb Q_v$, such that: for every ring isomorphism $\psi$ from $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ onto the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q_v,a,b]$ over $\mathbb Q_v$ which sends $z\otimes r$ to $r$ times the quaternion with coordinates the images of the coordinates of $z$, one has $\mathrm{nrd}(\psi(s))=1$; and $s=c\otimes 1+N\cdot z$ for some $z$ again in [`Submodule.localBox Λ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40).
--
--   This is the local determinant-correction step at a place of $\mathbb Q$ where $B$ splits: in a matrix model of the completed maximal order one adjusts an element whose reduced norm is a unit congruent to $1$ modulo $N$ into one of reduced norm exactly $1$ without changing it modulo $N$. It feeds the strong-approximation style statement [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_isUnitOf_nrd_eq_one_sub_mem_of_nrd_eq`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_isUnitOf_nrd_eq_one_sub_mem_of_nrd_eq), and cites the matrix model of the local box together with the identification of the reduced norm with the determinant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsMaximalOrder_exists_mem_localBox_nrd_eq_one_eq_tmul_add_smul.lean

